Two-Agent vs Multi-Agent Systems

In Agentic AI, an agent is an AI program that can make decisions, use tools, and perform tasks to achieve a goal.

The main difference between Two-Agent and Multi-Agent systems is how many agents collaborate.

| Feature          | Two-Agent System   | Multi-Agent System                      |
| ---------------- | ------------------ | --------------------------------------- |
| Number of Agents | 2                  | 3 or more                               |
| Complexity       | Simple             | More complex                            |
| Collaboration    | Between two agents | Among many specialized agents           |
| Best For         | Small tasks        | Large, real-world workflows             |
| Communication    | Direct             | Coordinated by rules or a manager agent |


1. Two-Agent System

A Two-Agent System has two AI agents working together.

Each agent has a different responsibility.

