Summary

| Aspect            | Two-Agent                    | Multi-Agent                               |
| ----------------- | ---------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| Number of Agents  | 2                            | 3 or more                                 |
| Task Distribution | Split between two agents     | Divided among many specialized agents     |
| Communication     | Direct between two agents    | Many agents communicate and collaborate   |
| Complexity        | Low                          | High                                      |
| Scalability       | Limited                      | High                                      |
| Best Use Cases    | Small applications, learning | Complex AI assistants, enterprise systems |


=======

In short:

A Two-Agent System is like two teammates working together on one task.
A Multi-Agent System is like an entire team where each member has a specialized role, collaborating to solve more complex problems.

